{"step_index":1895,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-29T03:34:06Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"VBScript silent launcher for Spectra with zero console window and NetworkAdapter process disguise.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"Set WshShell = CreateObject(\"WScript.Shell\")\nSet fso = CreateObject(\"Scripting.FileSystemObject\")\n\n' Set working directory to the directory of this script\nscriptDir = fso.GetParentFolderName(WScript.ScriptFullName)\nWshShell.CurrentDirectory = scriptDir\n\n' Camouflage Python executable as NetworkAdapter.exe\npythonwPath = \"venv\\Scripts\\pythonw.exe\"\nadapterPath = \"venv\\Scripts\\NetworkAdapter.exe\"\n\nIf fso.FileExists(pythonwPath) Then\n    If Not fso.FileExists(adapterPath) Then\n        fso.CopyFile pythonwPath, adapterPath, True\n    End If\n    ' Launch hidden (0) without waiting (False)\n    WshShell.Run \"\"\"\" & adapterPath & \"\"\" main.py\", 0, False\nElse\n    ' Fallback to system pythonw if no venv\n    WshShell.Run \"pythonw main.py\", 0, False\nEnd If\n","Description":"Create Spectra_Silent.vbs launcher with zero console window and NetworkAdapter disguise.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\Spectra_Silent.vbs","toolAction":"Creating Spectra_Silent.vbs","toolSummary":"Create Spectra_Silent.vbs"}}]}
{"step_index":1897,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-29T03:34:10Z","thinking":"**Considering File Output**\n\nI've realized `write_to_file` needs `TargetFile` in the project root, but seems agnostic to `ArtifactMetadata`, unless it's for brain artifacts. Now, the approach is to leverage `run_command` to generate `Spectra_Silent.vbs` and `spectra_silent.bat` instead.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"@'\nSet WshShell = CreateObject(\"WScript.Shell\")\nSet fso = CreateObject(\"Scripting.FileSystemObject\")\n\nscriptDir = fso.GetParentFolderName(WScript.ScriptFullName)\nWshShell.CurrentDirectory = scriptDir\n\npythonwPath = \"venv\\Scripts\\pythonw.exe\"\nadapterPath = \"venv\\Scripts\\NetworkAdapter.exe\"\n\nIf fso.FileExists(pythonwPath) Then\n    If Not fso.FileExists(adapterPath) Then\n        fso.CopyFile pythonwPath, adapterPath, True\n    End If\n    WshShell.Run \"\"\"\" & adapterPath & \"\"\" main.py\", 0, False\nElse\n    WshShell.Run \"pythonw main.py\", 0, False\nEnd If\n'@ | Set-Content -Path \"Spectra_Silent.vbs\" -Encoding ASCII\n\n@'\n@echo off\ncd /d \"%~dp0\"\nif exist \"venv\\Scripts\\pythonw.exe\" (\n    if not exist \"venv\\Scripts\\NetworkAdapter.exe\" (\n        copy /y \"venv\\Scripts\\pythonw.exe\" \"venv\\Scripts\\NetworkAdapter.exe\" >nul 2>&1\n    )\n    start \"\" \"venv\\Scripts\\NetworkAdapter.exe\" main.py\n) else (\n    start \"\" pythonw main.py\n)\nexit\n'@ | Set-Content -Path \"spectra_silent.bat\" -Encoding ASCII","Cwd":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Creating Spectra_Silent.vbs and spectra_silent.bat","toolSummary":"Create silent launchers"}}]}
